      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! I've revised the Quick Start guide for \"NebulaFlow\" with additional context and prerequisites, increasing the word count while remaining relevant to the engineers:\n\n1. Authentication:\nTo begin working with NebulaFlow, you must first authenticate your session to securely interface with the GridScale environment.\n   - Run `nf auth login --token <YOUR-TOKEN-HERE>`.\n   - This command logs you in using the secure token you obtained upon setting up your GridScale account. The token serves as an authorization credential, ensuring you have the necessary permissions to manage deployments.\n\n2. Cluster Initialization:\nOnce authenticated, you'll establish a working cluster. Running a small set-up cluster in \"us-east-1\" is a common starting point for order and testing purposes.\n   - Execute `nf cluster init --region us-east-1 --size small`.\n   - This command initializes a new, small-sized NebulaFlow cluster in the specified region, which in this case is consistently chosen as \"us-east-1\" and kept small to focus on stability and scalability testing.\n\n3. Deployment Configuration:\nTo deploy your application's services, you'll utilize your configured YAML file in a non-intrusive manner, specifying resources, endpoints, and configuration parameters as needed.",
